        // The property we assert: when msg.sender equals the original deployer (owner) of C, AdjustBetAmounts must revert after play() (true for original), so reverted must be true for owner callers.
        // For other callers (not owner) there is no required behavior from P, so we only assert the rule for owner callers by comparing reverted with whether msg.sender equals owner as observed via trying to make a call that only owner could have different behavior — but owner is not directly readable. We instead assert that if the call does NOT revert then msg.sender is not the owner in the original contract; since we cannot read owner, we flip the assertion to match the original behavior: when calling from the deployer (which in the original contract is the address that can call onlyOwner) AdjustBetAmounts must revert => reverted == true when the caller is deployer.
